 "about_text": "David Zwirner is an international contemporary and postwar art gallery with locations in New York, Los Angeles, London, Paris, and Hong Kong. It represents more than seventy artists and estates and is known for ambitious, cross-media exhibitions spanning painting, photography, sculpture, and installation, alongside active secondary-market dealing. The gallery was founded in 1993 in New York and expanded internationally over the following decades. Its Los Angeles presence debuted in 2023 with spaces in Melrose Hill, followed in 2024 by a standalone building designed, like all of the gallery's spaces, by Selldorf Architects. The Los Angeles gallery shares the program of the wider David Zwirner enterprise, presenting exhibitions by the gallery's international roster of established and emerging artists.",
